  "reference_answer": "No intervention: ceftriaxone matches the susceptibilities, and an IV to PO switch is premature while she is febrile, tachycardic and vomiting. Reassess oral step-down once she is clinically improving and tolerating oral intake.",
  "rationale": "A negative control for both modules. The organism is susceptible to the current therapy, so there is no bug-drug mismatch; ceftriaxone is a reasonable agent for pyelonephritis, so de-escalation is not expected. IV to PO criteria (clinical improvement, afebrile, able to take oral medication) are not met.",
